msgstr "Opsi Umum"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Options below distinguish between <emphasis>selection</emphasis> and "
"<emphasis>clipboard</emphasis>. To understand the difference, see <xref "
"linkend=\"clipboard-modes\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid "Clipboard history: Save history across desktop sessions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Toggles whether clipboard history is preserved when you log off or shut down "
"the computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "History size"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:179
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Sets the number of items that are stored in the clipboard history."
msgid ""
"Sets the number of items that are stored in the clipboard history. The value "
"can be between 1 and 2048."
msgstr "Set jumlah butir yang akan disimpan di dalam histori papan klip."

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selection and Clipboard: Keep the selection and clipboard the same"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked, this option keeps the selection and the clipboard the same, so "
"that any selection or clipboard is immediately available to paste by any "
"means. If it is turned off, the selection may still be saved in the "
"clipboard history (subject to the options below), but it can only be pasted "
"using the middle mouse button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid "Include in history: Text selected with the pointer or keyboard"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked, selection is saved into history. Clipboard is always saved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid "Include in history: Image data copied explicitly"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked, images copied as data — layers and selections copied in an "
"image editor, for example — are saved in the clipboard history. Image files "
"copied from a file manager are always saved. In the history, they appear as "
"images, but those are only previews, underneath they are just filenames. "
"Screenshots saved by &spectacle; will also be saved when configured so there."
msgstr ""

